    "body": "## Summary\n\n`bun audit` now reports no vulnerable JavaScript packages.\nThis change forces the transitive `lodash` dependency to resolve to `4.18.1`.\nThe override is needed because `concurrently` still allows the older vulnerable `lodash` range.\n\n## What Changed\n\nThe dependency change is small and limited to the root JavaScript package setup.\nIt does not change application code.\n\n- Added a root `package.json` override for `lodash`.\n- Updated `bun.lockb` so Bun resolves the dependency to the patched version.\n\n## Testing\n\nI ran Bun's dependency audit against this checkout.\nIt reported no vulnerabilities.\n\n- `bun audit`\n\nThe repository pre-push hook also ran the standard Rust checks before pushing.\n\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings -A deprecated`\n- `cargo test --workspace`\n- `cargo build --release --bin keycast`\n\n## Risks\n\nRisk is low because this only affects JavaScript dependency resolution.\nThe affected dependency is pulled through dev tooling, not the Rust application runtime.\n\n- No production deployment was performed.",
